From 19f3ac1e214c5a4e7231a3256f4e9ba1db23a61e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 05:54:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PUBLISH-FIX-115: the 13-second blocks get a name, and a
 nursery they can die in

Deployment 3047a8da (FIX-114 live) ran at 55-67% busy and still held the main
thread ~13 s about once every ten minutes: the minute tick printed 5.3 s late,
the watchdog saw 5 s of no heartbeat, the heap fell 1313 -> 558 MB in the same
minute, and at 01:45 the same shape ended in LAG_SUSTAINED shedding six pairs.
The watchdog's stack capture can only land after the collector releases the
thread, so it named ordinary work.

- lib/gc-report.js (diagnostic, authority NONE): every GC pause >= 250 ms on
  its own line (kind, duration, heap), the minute's collections as one line,
  from perf_hooks 'gc' entries. On unless SERPENT_GC_REPORT=false.
- .replit: NODE_OPTIONS adds --max-semi-space-size=64 (V8 default 16 MB) so
  the tens of MB/s of short-lived objects the book rate produces can die young
  instead of being promoted and collected by a full mark-compact. The heap
  ceiling and the run line are unchanged and fenced.

No frozen byte changed.

